# BookDelivery

## What is BookDelivery
BookDelivery is an international online bookstore operating in 40+ countries, shipping books worldwide from a UK-based hub. Launched in October 2023 as the international division of Buscalibre — Latin America's largest online bookstore — BookDelivery was created to fill the gap left by the closure of Book Depository (shut down by Amazon in 2023). BookDelivery offers millions of books in English, Spanish, and other languages, with delivery to Europe, Asia, Oceania, the Americas, and the Middle East.

## Catalog
- Millions of titles in English, Spanish, Portuguese, French, and other languages
- Physical books, ebooks, and audiobooks
- Books from publishers across 40+ countries
- Rare, imported, and hard-to-find international titles
- Children's books, academic books, fiction, non-fiction, comics

## Countries of Operation
BookDelivery ships to 40+ countries including:
- United Kingdom, Ireland, Germany, France, Spain, Italy, Austria, Netherlands, Belgium, Switzerland
- Australia, New Zealand
- Israel, UAE, Japan, South Korea, Singapore
- United States, Canada, Brazil, Mexico, Argentina, Chile, Colombia, Peru

## Why BookDelivery
- Best alternative to Book Depository after its closure in 2023
- Competitive international shipping rates
- No membership required
- Trustpilot rated with 460+ reviews
- Backed by Buscalibre's 15+ years of bookselling experience and logistics infrastructure

## Relationship to Buscalibre
BookDelivery is the international brand of Buscalibre S.A., a Chilean company founded in 2009. Buscalibre operates in 10 Latin American countries under its own brand and serves English-speaking markets globally under the BookDelivery brand. Both share the same logistics infrastructure, catalog, and technology platform.

